This program was written in python3. In limited testing it seems to work with Python2 as well.

To run with an explicit version, use "python2" or "python3" instead of simply "python" when executing.

To run the program simply execute: "python interpolation.py" for random generation of numbers 
OR 
execute "python interpolation.py <filename>" to pull from a file with x values on first row and f(x) on second row.

Included is an example file with a set of points in it, feel free to use it or not. To run the given file, for example, you would execute 'python interpolation.py exampleSet'